# Aquinas's reply suggests that "principle" might shift. Nature and will could be principles only as proximate causes, not as first causes. But each claim reads the same way in every statement that uses it. A1 joins reduction to nature and will with being "accounted for by other principles" in a single explanatory sense, so I see no bridge.
